  "sha_mismatch_explanation": {
    "note": "The rebuilt keep binaries match run8's sizes and every section size exactly, but their sha256 differs. Cause (verified on cue): BoringSSL C sources are compiled with __FILE__ paths pointing into the target dir \u2014 145 occurrences of the target-dir path in the binary's strings; they survive stripping because they are .rodata string literals, not debug info. This rebuild used /tmp/perf-fix1-target while run8 used /tmp/perf-full-target; both path strings are 21 chars, so sizes match exactly while bytes differ. Corroboration: the no-keep binary links no boring-sys, contains 0 target-dir strings, and reproduces run8's sha256 exactly. See byte_reproduction_check for the follow-up rebuild with the run8 target-dir name.",
